  "version": "1.1.0",
  "updated_at": "2026-10-17",
  "change_note": "The test run on the market day of October sixteen recorded nothing: eight outlets on the list make every search fail, and CNBC and Bloomberg pages refuse to open. Those eight move to blocked; outlets and official sources our tools can open are added; each host says whether it opens.",
  "reach_checked": "2026-10-17",
  "rules": [
    "Link only to the hosts in sources or their subdomains. Anything else, every host under blocked included, is refused when the note is recorded.",
    "Search with allowed_domains set to the hosts marked search true, never a blocked host: one host that refuses automated search makes the whole search fail.",
    "Prefer official sources: the company, a regulator, a newswire release, and for a market-wide move official data (EIA or OPEC for oil, the Fed, BLS or BEA for rates and data releases, the exchanges).",
    "Add a reputable outlet that explains the move. A wire story republished in full on a listed host (AP on PBS or ABC News, Reuters on Yahoo Finance or NBC News) counts as that host's page.",
    "A page that will not open (an error, a login, a subscription or a bot check) is skipped; look for the same story on another listed host. Never a cache, archive, mirror, proxy or reader copy.",
    "A source counts only when its page was opened and supports the claim; a search snippet is never a source. Read each host's note before citing it.",
    "Write the note in your own words: no quotation marks, no copied sentences, no digits, no prices or price targets.",
    "Every source must be dated on or before the market day plus one day.",
    "When no listed page that opens explains the move, record an unclear note that says so plainly; it may have no source.",
    "A note explains a move. It is never a reason to buy or sell."
  ],
